        "Content": "6 New Street, Carrick on Suir, Co Tipperary E32 WR52\r\n\r\nFor Sale by Live Virtual Online & Public Auction\r\n\r\nWednesday 28th of October 2026 \r\n\r\nAt\r\n\r\nWilsons Auctions, Kingswood Interchange, Naas Road, Dublin 22\r\n\r\nExcellent Investment Opportunity\r\n\r\nLocation Clonmel 21km, Waterford 27km, Kilkenny 41km, Dublin 164km. \r\n\r\nThe property is superbly located centrally in Carrick-on-Suir town. Population (2022) 5,752. Carrick-on Suir lies on both banks of the River Suir and it has an unusual characteristic of being in two counties, Tipperary and Waterford. Situated on New Street, this property enjoys a prominent central position with strong footfall and immediate access to shops, cafés, schools, public services, and transport links. CarrickonSuir is a vibrant heritage town benefiting from ongoing regeneration and strong local demand. CarrickonSuir is well connected to Clonmel, Waterford City, and Kilkenny, making it an attractive location for owneroccupiers, investors, and businesses alike. The town's combination of historical charm and modern amenities continues to attract strong interest.\r\n\r\nDescription TY66115F\r\n\r\nThe subject property was formally a mixed use 2 story mid terrace dwelling. The property believed to date pre 1900 extends to c.117.55 sq. m 1,265 sq. ft. The property currently contains 2 apartments. The accommodation for the larger apartment comprises of a kitchen, sitting room, 3 bedrooms and a family bathroom over two floors. The smaller apartment comprises of a kitchen, bedroom and bathroom at ground floor level. To the rear of the property is a very long enclosed garden and yard containing out buildings. The property requires refurbishment. This well-located town centre building offers a strong combination of commercial visibility and residential accommodation, making it an ideal investment or owner occupier opportunity.\r\n\r\nBER E1 # 111476933\r\n\r\nViewing - By appointment \r\n\r\nSolicitor State Solicitor, Chief State Solicitor's Office, Osmond House, Little Ship Street, Dublin 8\r\n\r\nVAT Refer to legal contracts."
